# Production prompt overlay (auto-discovered, or VRAKSHA_PROMPTS_DIR). The real,
# hardened prompts for EVERY llm call (verifier/filter/orchestrator/memory +
# experts' system.md and skills) live here.
#
# NOW COMMITTED (owner decision, 2026-08-01). It was ignored to keep prompts out of
# a leak, but the repo is private and a leak of it exposes security/, core/, and
# every invariant anyway -- the prompts were the least sensitive thing in here. The
# cost of ignoring them was concrete and daily: no backup (one copy on one disk), no
# history, no rollback, no reviewable diff for security-relevant prompt edits, and
# CI validating prompts/ while production ran prompts.secure/ -- a green suite
# proving things about a prompt nobody runs.
#
# They still are NOT baked into the image (see backend/.dockerignore and
# backend/Dockerfile) and are supplied at deploy time. Nothing about the runtime
# overlay contract changed; only their provenance did.
#
# Keep them free of credentials and of any individual's name or location -- they are
# instructions, not secrets. Anything that IS a secret belongs in .env, never here.
*.secure/
secure.*/
!prompts.secure/
!prompts.secure/**

security/vendors/

demos/
drafts/
/backend-audit/notes/*
!/backend-audit/notes/README.md
!/backend-audit/drafts/
/backend-audit/drafts/*
!/backend-audit/drafts/README.md
/benchmarks/        # anchored: root-level only, so docs/benchmarks/ stays tracked

/memory/

