# conversation/ was updated to:
# `reports/*`, not `reports/` — git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so a `!` re-include for a file inside it is silently dead. Excluding the
# contents instead keeps the directory walkable and the exception live.
reports/*
# ...except the Integration Contract. It is not a report — it is the shared
# backend↔frontend source of truth both agents read, CB6's artifact, and Phase
# 4's whole deliverable. Everything else in reports/ is per-agent depth that a
# fresh clone does not need; this one a fresh clone cannot work without. Same
# durability logic as .agents/provider-handoffs/ above.
!reports/INTEGRATION_CONTRACT.md
handoff.*
HANDOFF.*
# Kuzu embedded graph DB (GraphPort backing store) — never commit the db files
backend/core/memory/data/

# Owner-only compliance reports (personal, never committed)

